      "content": "wait, the code you wrote for the \"inplace\" part looks the same as the one that causes the warning... i think there's a typo there. also, you mentioned \"editing the DataFrame in the scope it was first created\" but that's kind of vague. can you explain the actual difference between a view and a copy? like, why does pandas get confused about whether it's looking at the original data or a new one?",
      "source": "evaluator"
